ssions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nHey @bluebill1049 ! Me and my team just got started with RHF a few days ago and loving the adoption so far. But one of our use cases demands having a \"defaultValues\" prop being received from parent components dynamically (changing over the user interaction cycle). Setting it initially such as `useForm({defaultValues: initialValues})`, initialValues being the prop, doesn't reflect the initial values correctly, so I tried using 'reset' within a useEffect hook, but run into a **re-render loop**.\r\nThis looks like the same issue described in https://github.com/react-hook-form/react-hook-form/issues/126 \r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n\r\n1. Open the CodeSandbox example and add 'reset' as a dependency where I placed the comment.\r\n2. A re-render loop should be triggered\r\n\r\n**Codesandbox link (Required)**\r\n\r\nhttps://codesandbox.io/s/react-hook-form-reset-form-forked-14dse?file=/src/index.js\r\n\r\nWe really appreciate any input as having defaultValues in place is mandatory and couldn't figure it out. \r\nApart from that, cheers to a great library!\r\n\r\n**Desktop (please complete the following information):**\r\n\r\n- OS: Ubuntu\r\n- Browser: Chrome 85\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nAdd any other context about the problem here.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react-hook-form/react-hook-form/issues/3587/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react-hook-form/react-hook-form/issues/3587/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":7596714871,"node_id":"LOE_lADOCl-cD84b1T6vzwAAAAHEzKt3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react-hook-form/react-hook-form/issues/events/7596714871","actor":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898